  "solution": {
    "approach": "Strip country code '91' if 12 digits, then split into two 5-digit halves and swap.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\nint main() {\n    char s[105]; if (scanf(\"%s\", s) != 1) return 0;\n    char *p = s;\n    if (strlen(s) == 12 && s[0] == '9' && s[1] == '1') p = s + 2;\n    printf(\"%s\", p + 5);\n    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) putchar(p[i]);\n    putchar('\\n');\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    string s; if (!(cin >> s)) return 0;\n    if (s.length() == 12 && s.rfind(\"91\", 0) == 0) s = s.substr(2);\n    cout << s.substr(5) << s.substr(0, 5) << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNext()) {\n            String s = sc.next();\n            if (s.length() == 12 && s.startsWith(\"91\")) s = s.substring(2);\n            System.out.println(s.substring(5) + s.substring(0, 5));\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\ndef main():\n    toks = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if toks:\n        s = toks[0]\n        if len(s) == 12 and s.startswith(\"91\"): s = s[2:]\n        print(s[5:] + s[:5])\nif __name__ == \"__main__\": main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require(\"fs\");\nfunction main() {\n    const toks = fs.readFileSync(0, \"utf-8\").trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (toks && toks[0]) {\n        let s = toks[0];\n        if (s.length === 12 && s.startsWith(\"91\")) s = s.slice(2);\n        console.log(s.slice(5) + s.slice(0, 5));\n    }\n}\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "If length is 12 and starts with '91', take last 10 digits. Print s[5:] + s[:5]."
  },
